[code snippet 1]
This code snippet demonstrates an improper use of the Java API that can make an application vulnerable. It shows a potential security risk by not properly handling user input.  
This is a vulnerable example that could expose sensitive data.  
***  
To fix this, always validate and sanitize user inputs before processing them.

```java
// Improper code that can be vulnerable
String userInput = request.getParameter("username");
String query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '" + userInput + "'";
```

***  
The corrected version ensures proper input handling and prevents potential vulnerabilities.  
This improved code avoids the risk by using parameterized queries.

```java
// Fixed code to avoid vulnerabilities
String userInput = request.getParameter("username");
String query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?";
PreparedStatement pstmt = connection.prepareStatement(query);
pstmt.setString(1, userInput);
ResultSet results = pstmt.executeQuery();
```

